async: never post the no-apc_context completion packet to a socket

Branch C (NEUTRON FIX v3) posts add_async_completion(async, 0, ...) -- an IOCP packet
whose lpOverlapped is NULL. Windows never posts one: the kernel posts only when
ApcContext != NULL, and kernelbase's ReadFile encodes the rule as
  if (((ULONG_PTR)overlapped->hEvent & 1) == 0) cvalue = overlapped;

The 32-bit CLR's ThreadpoolMgr::CompletionPortDispatchWorkWithinAppDomain reads
lpOverlapped-8 with no NULL check, so any .NET app doing socket receives on a
threadpool port dies with c0000005 / 80131506 (COR_E_EXECUTIONENGINE).

Synchronous socket recv is exactly what reaches this branch: ws2_32's WS2_recv_base
passes apc=NULL and apc_context=NULL when no OVERLAPPED is supplied. The libuv/UXP
traffic the branch was written for is pipes and devices, which this does not touch.
Regular files never reach it at all -- NtReadFile handles them in-process and posts
client-side with a correct cvalue.

Measured before shipping: with the packet suppressed entirely, Premiere's home screen
rendered FULL and its stability was unchanged across three control runs, while the
aescripts manager stopped crashing. Keeping the branch for non-sockets preserves
whatever it does for Premiere and removes the .NET fault.

--- a/server/async.c
+++ b/server/async.c
@@ -629,6 +629,16 @@
              * Reuses add_async_completion() (no-ops if the fd has no completion port). Honors
              * FILE_SKIP_COMPLETION_PORT_ON_SUCCESS like the path above. cvalue 0. */
             else if (!async->data.apc && !async->data.apc_context && async->fd &&
+                     /* NEUTRON 2026-09-06: NEVER to a socket. This branch posts cvalue 0, i.e. an
+                      * IOCP packet with a NULL lpOverlapped, which Windows never posts. The 32-bit
+                      * CLR's CompletionPortDispatchWorkWithinAppDomain reads lpOverlapped-8 with no
+                      * NULL check and dies (c0000005 / 80131506) -- any .NET app doing Socket
+                      * receives on a threadpool port. Sync socket recv is exactly what reaches here
+                      * (ws2_32 passes apc=NULL, apc_context=NULL); the libuv/UXP traffic this branch
+                      * was written for is pipes and devices, which are unaffected. Measured: an A/B
+                      * with this packet suppressed left Premiere's home screen FULL and its
+                      * stability unchanged over 3 control runs. See docs/wiki/AESCRIPTS-MANAGER.md. */
+                     get_fd_type( async->fd ) != FD_TYPE_SOCKET &&
                      (async->pending || !(async->comp_flags & FILE_SKIP_COMPLETION_PORT_ON_SUCCESS)))
             {
                 /* NEUTRON: debug trace OFF by default — this branch runs on every libuv/IOCP
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -2176,6 +2176,14 @@
     return !(fd->options & (FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_ALERT | FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT));
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON: the fd's server-side type, or FD_TYPE_INVALID when this fd_ops has no
+ * get_fd_type (change.c's named_pipe_dir passes NULL). Exposed so async.c can keep
+ * its no-apc_context completion packet away from sockets -- see async_terminate(). */
+enum server_fd_type get_fd_type( struct fd *fd )
+{
+    return fd->fd_ops->get_fd_type ? fd->fd_ops->get_fd_type( fd ) : FD_TYPE_INVALID;
+}
+
 /* retrieve the unix fd for an object */
 int get_unix_fd( struct fd *fd )
 {
--- a/server/file.h
+++ b/server/file.h
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@
 extern unsigned int get_fd_options( struct fd *fd );
 extern unsigned int get_fd_comp_flags( struct fd *fd );
 extern int is_fd_overlapped( struct fd *fd );
+extern enum server_fd_type get_fd_type( struct fd *fd );
 extern int get_unix_fd( struct fd *fd );
 extern client_ptr_t get_fd_map_address( struct fd *fd );
 extern void set_fd_map_address( struct fd *fd, client_ptr_t addr, mem_size_t size );
